foundation.question_text:
The weighted network shows connections between four vertices $A, B, C, D$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (3.2,2.5);
\coordinate (C) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above] {$3$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$5$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$2$};
\draw (D) -- (A) node[midway, left] {$6$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use Prim's algorithm starting at vertex $A$ to find the minimum spanning tree and calculate its total weight.

