mastery.question_text:
The diagram shows a $7$-vertex weighted network with $13$ edges.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.5);
\coordinate (C) at (2,0.5);
\coordinate (G) at (3.5,2);
\coordinate (D) at (5,3.5);
\coordinate (E) at (5,0.5);
\coordinate (F) at (7,2);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$4$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, below left] {$6$};
\draw (A) -- (G) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$5$};
\draw (B) -- (G) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw (C) -- (G) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$2$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[midway, above] {$3$};
\draw (G) -- (D) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$5$};
\draw (G) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw (C) -- (E) node[midway, below] {$6$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$7$};
\draw (D) -- (F) node[midway, above right] {$5$};
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway, below right] {$3$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$C$};
\fill (G) circle (2.5pt) node[above=2pt] {$G$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Apply Prim's algorithm systematically from vertex $A$ to find the complete minimum spanning tree.
